# The two ABox forms, and exactly those: C(a) and r(a,b).
# C(a) -> the GCI individual(a) subseteq C; r(a,b) -> an EDGE, not an existential.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:C a owl:Class . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :C .
:b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:a :r :b .
